in King you control a group of warriors  each with different skills and abilities  how you choose to equip and improve them  makes all the difference between  surviving long enough to take out all  the bosses and unravel the mysteries of  this world or not at the start of the  game you have two warriors that you  control RAM and Ulrich and then others  join as you play through for a total of  six this makes up your pack of warriors  but alas as we all know not all six  packs ha created equal so here are the  top four things you need to know to make  the most of your six pack each warrior  has three abilities that you can bestow  upon them mind body and control  increasing mind will turn the hero into  a formidable magician strengthening the  body will make your hero a powerful  warrior and control turns your hero into  a cunning coordinated ranger or assassin  in King you are free to rebalance your  hero abilities whenever you are not in  combat so you can adjust to any  situation kin throws your way each  ability has a specific skill tree when  you complete a mission you are awarded  points and these can be spent against  abilities for each 15 points invested in  an ability you unlock a new tier of  skills basic skills range from healing  spells to tactical crowd control or all  around may  in the game there is a special skill  slot reserved for feed skills feed  skills are formed by combining a feed  stone with certain skills like their  name suggests feed stones feed on  specific energies in the world for  example the deathstone feeds on death  while the life stone feeds on life you  can unleash the powerful feed skill once  the stone is full feed stones range from  quite common to extremely rare and tough  to obtain a true hero needs armor and  weapons that complement his abilities if  for some reason you can't find the  equipment you need on the stinking  corpse of a deceased enemy you are  always free to craft your own each piece  of equipment in the world can be crafted  by finding the right components there  are over 90 crafting components  available thus even the most picky hero  can create something he likes  armor and weapons aside what's the point  in having a great-looking six-pack if  you don't know how to use it properly  while most enemies don't look  particularly intelligent they can make  your life harder than you would expect  so working your warriors as a team is  paramount to surviving some of the  trickier enemies you'll face if your  efforts are just not paying off and you  find yourself falling short then there's  only one option slow down time that's  more like it the advantage of tactical  time manipulation it makes all the  difference so there you have it a few  little hints on how to make the most of  your six-pack adventure on drave  adventurer kin is calling
 

